   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## A1111 Loopback\n\nThis is what people remember as A1111's colour correction being \"built into sampling\". It is not: the webui has no correction inside its sampler. It is the Loopback script.\n\nEach pass is a full img2img, so the **content** is reworked every time — that is why it looks like more than a colour filter. What stays fixed is the reference: measured once from the starting image and reused by every pass, so the palette cannot drift however long the chain runs.\n\n- `denoise` falls from the first pass to `final_denoise`, so the chain settles instead of wandering.\n- `hold_exposure` is ours, not A1111's. Its blend takes lightness from the generated image, so a long chain holds colour but can still wander brighter or darker. Raise this if yours does.\n- Wire a `mask` to rework only part of the frame: everything outside is pasted back from the original after each pass, so it does not soften.\n\n`all_passes` is every pass as a batch — scrub it to see the progression."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
